{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1559615-police-tactics-third-dot-another-grappling-thread","id":1559615,"title":"Police Tactics Third Dot - another grappling thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-04-25T10:15:15-07:00","id":1559615,"title":"Police Tactics Third Dot - another grappling thread","content":"I'm looking to create a mortal character for a HtV game so I've been rereading the combat rules. Which lead me to the police tactics fighting style and the confusion over the word immobilized. Has there ever been a clear cut answer?<br /> <br /> Grappling seems to go with a sequence of three steps - initiate grapple, apply Hold, and then apply Restrain which grants the Immobilized Tilt. Restrain can either be joint locks or cuffs/ties; both forms are mentioned as if making a successful Restrain is enough to use the retaining tools if you have them.<br /> <br /> Police Tactics grants reflexive use of cuffs or ties if you have them to an immobilized opponent. Does that mean they have to have the Immobilized Tilt or is a Hold enough? My assumption, based on making the merit dot worth something, is that applying Hold is enough to invoke a reflective success on Restrain. But as written that word immobilized is awkward since it is also the name of a specific Tilt that only applies after Restrain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28478-madmarcus","name":"Madmarcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-25T10:56:18-07:00","id":1559616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madmarcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1559615-police-tactics-third-dot-another-grappling-thread#post1559615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking to create a mortal character for a HtV game so I've been rereading the combat rules. Which lead me to the police tactics fighting style and the confusion over the word immobilized. Has there ever been a clear cut answer?<br /> <br /> Grappling seems to go with a sequence of three steps - initiate grapple, apply Hold, and then apply Restrain which grants the Immobilized Tilt. Restrain can either be joint locks or cuffs/ties; both forms are mentioned as if making a successful Restrain is enough to use the retaining tools if you have them.<br /> <br /> Police Tactics grants reflexive use of cuffs or ties if you have them to an immobilized opponent. Does that mean they have to have the Immobilized Tilt or is a Hold enough? My assumption, based on making the merit dot worth something, is that applying Hold is enough to invoke a reflective success on Restrain. But as written that word immobilized is awkward since it is also the name of a specific Tilt that only applies after Restrain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that Restrain requires an action to perform and one of the example is applying handcuffs, it would be reasonable to think that a 4th dot merit could grant you the possibility to Restrain on the same turn of a successful Hold","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-25T11:33:56-07:00","id":1559617,"title":"","content":"Police Tactics/Subdual has the disadvantage of being written back when the mechanics were meant to be adjustments to 1e instead of a formal new edition; 1e's version of the grappling rules didn't differentiate between the Hold and Immobilize maneuvers, while the distinction between drawing/controlling a weapon and using it to deal damage was preserved (albeit streamlined to combine the &quot;draw weapon&quot; and &quot;turn a drawn weapon&quot; actions into &quot;control weapon&quot;).<br /> <br /> The newest iteration of the mechanics for Handcuffs in Deviant's Clade Companion switch the earlier description of using a mechanically different roll to apply the cuffs to simply having it be part of the Restrain move, so the practical reading (avoiding the need to make too many assumptions about how having restraints &quot;drawn&quot; affect your Initiative and dicepools) would seem to be that Speed Cuff allows you to treat the Restrain maneuver the same as the Break Free maneuver with appropriate use of equipment, i.e. if you succeed you can take another action immediately afterwards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-25T19:18:54-07:00","id":1559630,"title":"","content":"That makes a lot of mechanical sense. It also looks like it makes it a tad less effective; no change in your actions but you have the time from your Hold action until your next action that you are still grappled and without defense. <br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28478-madmarcus","name":"Madmarcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}